  "ui_validation": "AppTest edited RF/GBT class shift, model seeds, tree/iteration counts and learning rate; values persisted from Workloads back to Experiments.",
  "limitations": [
    "RF huge/gigantic/bigdata preset definitions and logical volume checked only; actual generation exercised RF tiny/small/large and all six GBT presets. Full YARN training used original tiny and explicitly customized fixtures only.",
    "RF native Spark ML averages leaf probabilities; the former model hard-voted tree labels. Four of 40 controlled five-tree predictions differed; leaf probability reference and repeatability passed. No universal identical-tree/metric/runtime claim.",
    "Split seed 11 now explicit; old splits were nondeterministic. RF model seed 1 now explicit; GBT effective seed 0 preserved. File/sample order may alter fitted models.",
    "Original row-seeded empirical Gaussian deviations are preserved; theoretical ideal moments are not substituted for the original reference.",
    "Parquet encoding, metadata and action/evaluation plans differ from ObjectFile; no historical throughput equivalence or performance superiority claimed.",
    "Original tiny contains ten rows; two held-out rows in this run are not a reliable quality estimate.",
    "Local verification ran during part of the YARN smoke campaign; timings are not a controlled performance study.",
    "Cloud/serverless platforms not certified."
  ],
  "correction_notes": [
    "Inspected runtime bytecode before final build: preserved RF bootstrap only when trees > 1 and GBT legacy model seed 0.",
    "Historical test adapter initially attempted a non-public two-argument GBT constructor; switched to the original public constructor, whose effective seed 0 was verified. Production code was unaffected.",
    "Initial universal prediction-equality assertion failed for RF; investigation established hard-versus-probability voting. Added an independent leaf-confidence oracle, retained native Spark ML behavior and documented algorithm revision.",
    "Removed duplicated pipe character from parameter character-class regex after Python FutureWarning; accepted characters unchanged."
  ],
